From af4bd408e591b6bb97d5d8cd9e6691b9e24d3327 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:47:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Late-game trainer evolutions, Trainer Tower hand-picked
 stand-ins, guide gift listings (R20)

- trainer_evolutions.py: every Lv. 50+ trainer Pokemon at least 5 levels
  past a level-up evolution evolves (68 Pokemon). postgame_levels.py had
  skipped evolutions whose species was already on the team.
- validate.py: flags any Lv. 50+ trainer Pokemon left unevolved.
- tower_sets.py: hand-picked stand-ins where the automatic pick broke a
  trainer's theme (Glaceon and Leafeon for the Eeveelution twins, Kingdra
  and Feraligatr for Shania, Ampharos for Owen, Dusknoir for Zackery).
- Spoiler guide: shared rewards are listed under every place that gives
  them, and the League rooms have their apostrophes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JQmLEZftLdDmGYX3wiQ71G
---
 HACK_NOTES.md                    |  10 +-
 include/hack_version.h           |   2 +-
 src/data/trainer_parties.h       | 183 +++++++++++++++++++------------
 src/trainer_tower_sets.c         | 100 ++++++++---------
 tools/hack/spoiler_guide.py      |  18 ++-
 tools/hack/tower_sets.py         |  21 +++-
 tools/hack/trainer_evolutions.py |  68 ++++++++++++
 tools/hack/validate.py           |  16 ++-
 8 files changed, 289 insertions(+), 129 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tools/hack/trainer_evolutions.py

diff --git a/HACK_NOTES.md b/HACK_NOTES.md
index dee7724..8bce5ee 100644
--- a/HACK_NOTES.md
+++ b/HACK_NOTES.md
@@ -553,6 +553,10 @@ teams are:
   - Trainer Pokémon evolve where their new level allows.
 - **Post-game route rematches:** VS Seeker rematch teams that unlock after
   the Champion are 1.25x stronger (about Lv. 66–86).
+- **Late-game evolutions:** every trainer Pokémon of Lv. 50 or higher has
+  evolved where its level allows (5 levels past the evolution), even if the
+  team already has one, e.g. no more Lv. 72 Mareep or Lv. 68 Magikarp.
+  Earlier trainers keep their classic unevolved Pokémon.
 - **Held items:** the Trainer Tower lobby shop on Seven Island also sells the
   held items competitive teams use: Leftovers, Choice Band, Shell Bell, Focus
   Band, Quick Claw, Scope Lens, Bright Powder, King's Rock, Lucky Egg, Metal
@@ -582,8 +586,9 @@ Each script runs once against the original pret data:
   an unused species slot, with its graphics, cry, Pokédex entry and evolution item.
 - `balance.py`: modern boss movesets, peak teams with the later evolutions.
 - `validate.py`: checks the game data for missing or inconsistent entries,
-  including that every peak team is six Lv. 100 Pokémon and every Trainer
-  Tower team is fully evolved with no repeated species or item.
+  including that every peak team is six Lv. 100 Pokémon, every Trainer
+  Tower team is fully evolved with no repeated species or item, and no
+  Lv. 50+ trainer Pokémon is left unevolved.
 - `playtest/playtest.py [check ...]`: automated playtest. It runs 25 milestone
   checks in a headless mGBA:
   - The boot menu.
@@ -609,6 +614,7 @@ Each script runs once against the original pret data:
   `gcc -O2 -w -o tools/hack/playtest/harness tools/hack/playtest/harness.c -lmgba`.
 - `held_item_shop.py`: held items in the Trainer Tower lobby shop and their prices.
 - `postgame_levels.py`: Sevii Islands 4–7 trainers and wild Pokémon, and post-game route rematches.
+- `trainer_evolutions.py`: Lv. 50+ trainer Pokémon evolve where their level allows (run after `postgame_levels.py`).
 - `tower_sets.py <dir>`: the competitive Trainer Tower teams, from Showdown's
   random-battle set files (read as data).
 - `gym_doubles.py`: the gym double battles (one trainer per gym) and their doubles movesets.
